  "final_answer_preview": "According to Section 318(2) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, whoever cheats shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to three years, or with fine, or with both. Furthermore, Section 318(3) states that if the cheating is done with the knowledge that it is likely to cause wrongful loss to a person whose interest the offender was bound to protect, the punishment may extend to five years, or with fine, or with both. Additionally, Section 319(2) specifies that cheating by personation is punishable with imprisonment for a term which may extend to five years, or with fine, or with both.",
